@startuml TTL8_Class_Diagram
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
class CPU {
  - A, B, IR, MAR : Register8
  - PC : uint8_t
  - carry, zero, halted : bool
  - bus : Bus
  - alu : ALU
  - memory : Memory
  - input : InputPort
  - outputPort : OutputPort
  + reset()
  + loadProgram(bytes, address)
  + step()
  + run(maxSteps)
}
class Register8 { +load(value) +clear() +read() }
class Bus { +write(data) +read() }
class ALU { +add(a,b) +subtract(a,b) +bitAnd(a,b) +bitOr(a,b) +bitXor(a,b) +bitNot(a) }
class Memory { +read(address) +write(address,value) +clear() }
class InputPort { +write(value) +read() +available() }
class OutputPort { +write(value) +value() +history() }
class ControlUnit { +decode(opcode) }
class ControlStore { +load(bytes,wordBytes,stepBits) +read(opcode,step) }
class ProgramCounter { +load(value) +increment() +read() }
class Flags { +carry : bool +zero : bool +updateZero(value) }
class Clock { +tick() +high() +edgeCount() }
CPU *-- Register8
CPU *-- Bus
CPU *-- ALU
CPU *-- Memory
CPU *-- InputPort
CPU *-- OutputPort
note right of CPU : Current CPU uses primitive PC and flag fields.
ProgramCounter ..> CPU : reusable component
Flags ..> CPU : reusable component
Clock ..> CPU : not yet cycle-integrated
ControlUnit ..> CPU : opcode decode model
ControlStore ..> CPU : separate ROM image model
@enduml
